WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.504
-Former president Donald Trump
will give his first speech

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.506
since leaving office
this weekend

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.641
at the Conservative
Political Action Conference,

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.110
and Republicans are still
rallying around him

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.346
as the future
and the leader of the GOP.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.648
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:19.752 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:21.120
After five years
of doing

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.555
everything possible
to hide them,

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.591
it was reported today that
Donald Trump was finally forced

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:27.827
to turn over his tax records
to the Manhattan

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.930
district attorney this week,
after the Supreme Court denied

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.132
his last-ditch attempt
to keep them concealed.

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:34.400
And look,
I'm no prosecutor,

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.536
but it can't be that hard
to find a crime

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.038
in the tax records of a guy
who claims to be a billionaire

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:42.641
yet paid only $750
in federal income taxes

00:00:42.641 --> 00:00:45.144
when he was president.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:46.512
It wasn't way back
in the '80's,

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:49.014
when he was just a New York
real estate developer

00:00:49.014 --> 00:00:53.986
and I'm guessing aspiring
birthday magician.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:57.323
"Mom, that guy made
my presents disappear."

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.492
This was 2017,
when he was the most powerful

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.860
and most famous person
in the world.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.362
It was so brazen I'm shocked he
didn't livestream it.

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.398
"'Sup, fam,
welcome to my Twitch stream.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.799
Today, we'll be committing
tax fraud.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.801
And make sure to subscribe,
because next week,

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.804
we'll be playing
the new online Ocean Master."

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:14.908
And yes, there are plenty
of technically legal ways

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.410
that the wealthy
and corporations avoid taxes,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.911
which is a scandal
in itself.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:22.014
But something tells me
Trump doesn't just limit himself

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:23.049
to the legal stuff.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.417
I'm guessing
he commits crimes

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.419
the way the rest of us
order apps for the table.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.621
"Let's just get -- should
we just get one of everything?"

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.257
So, a criminal investigation
in Manhattan is intensifying,

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:34.027
not to mention an investigation
in Georgia of his attempts

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.128
to steal the election there.

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:36.663
Plus, there are, like,
I don't know,

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:39.499
30 other investigations,
last I checked.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:42.101
Oh, and also, there was
that whole insurrection thing.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.636
And yet,
he's still scheduled

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:46.038
to give his first
post-presidency speech

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:48.975
to the Conservative Political
Action Conference on Sunday --

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.710
a move that has most
Republicans thrilled,

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.414
but also caused a few
awkward moments in the party,

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.515
as evidenced by
the public split yesterday

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:58.618
between House GOP leader
Kevin McCarthy

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.453
and Congresswoman
Liz Cheney,

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.589 line:0%
who voted
to impeach Trump.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:10.763 line:0%
-Yes. He should.

00:02:29.214 --> 00:02:30.683 line:0%
-On that high note...

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.984 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:34.320
-[ Fake laughs ]
Very funny.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.023
The GOP responds to divisions
over the future of their party

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.958
like an uncle who farts
at Thanksgiving dinner.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:43.363
"Oh. And with that, I will
retire to the family room."

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:46.132
It was rare to see that kind
of disunity on public display

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.300
because,
during his presidency,

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.368
Trump commanded
near-universal loyalty

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:52.705
within the Republican party,
despite his abysmal record

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.840
of failure
on both policy and politics.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.476
Remember, he never cracked
50% approval once,

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:00.113
he was impeached twice,
he lost the popular vote twice,

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.115
he lost the House
by the highest margin

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:04.350
since Watergate,
and lost the Senate in January

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.219
when Democrats
won two Senate seats.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.688
In what was once a reliably
red state, Georgia,

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.389
sticking with Trump
is like putting Ringo

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:11.691
in charge
of the Beatles.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:15.961
[As Ringo] "Okay. what about
more songs where I sing?

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:20.700
Also, a no autograph policy.
Peace and love."

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.468
[Normal voice]
Why on earth would you want
to stick with a guy

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.470
who's basically
single-handedly responsible

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.672
for your political
annihilation?

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:28.074
It reminds me of
my weekly bowling team.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:31.210
We would all hit at least 200
every week, except for Dale,

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.445
who would always chuck the ball
across two lanes

00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:36.015
because he had gravy all over
his hands from the disco fries.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.683
And every week,
I'd tell my teammates,

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.017
"Let's cut Dale loose."

00:03:39.017 --> 00:03:41.620
And they'd say, "We can't
because he bankrolls the team

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.689
with the million dollar
settlement he won from the local

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.991
Dairy Queen when he spilled
the blizzard in his lap

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:47.760
and his dog
got frostbite."

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.196
Anyway, the point is,
Republicans stuck by Trump

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.964
no matter how bad he was
for the party

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:53.165
because they agreed
with him.

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:55.101
They were engaged
in the same project,

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.269
and wanted
the same things.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.104
With a few exceptions,
they were all Trump.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:01.407
I mean, Lindsey Graham
literally wore the same clothes

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.543
when they went golfing,
like a Chihuahua

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.544
whose owner makes them wear
matching outfits.

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:07.646
This looks like one of those
pictures of Manute Bol

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:10.950
and Muggsy Bogues when they both
played for the Bullets.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.885
It was called "The Bullets"
before they changed it

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.954
to "The Wizards."

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:17.022
It took an armed insurrection
stoked by the president,

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:18.924
fueled by insane lies
about election fraud,

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:20.126
to finally
put some distance

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:22.195
between a few Republicans
and Trump.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.096
Even Graham,
as you might recall,

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:27.166
briefly suggested that
he might finally be ready

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.634 line:0%
to separate himself
from Trump.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:31.837 line:0%
-Trump and I, look, we've had
a hell of a journey.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.539 line:0%
I hate it
to end this way.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.107 line:0%
Oh, my God,
I hate it.

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:37.810 line:0%
From my point of view, he's been
a consequential president.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.814 line:0%
But today,
first thing you'll see,

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:45.351 line:0%
all I can say is
count me out.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.186 line:0%
Enough is enough.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.088
-I believe he was reciting
a monologue

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:53.359
from the Tennessee Williams play
"A Streetcar Named De-Liar."

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:54.927
You can stay for the rest
of the "Closer Look,"

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.262
but it's all downhill
from there.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.030
What's that?
You want me to do a scene

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.198
from "Streetcar named De-Liar"?

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.599
I couldn't. Okay.

00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:02.468
[Southern accent] We've had a
long journey, Trump and I,

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:05.004
from the salt marshes of
Charlton, to the river boats

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.573
of Mississippi,
to the Sparkleberry swamp.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:10.442
Meemaw says he's just a figment
of my imagination,

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:12.511
but to me,
he was real --

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:16.816
as real as a glass of peach tea
on a warm Chattanooga knight.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:19.819
God, I hate it to end this way,
but sometimes life comes up

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:23.422
and bites you, like an
Appalachian salamander
on a meth bender.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:24.757
[Normal voice]
And scene.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:29.261
Well, it won't surprise you
to learn that Graham

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:30.863
almost immediately
did a 180.

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.832
He probably thought that,
by calling out

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:36.802
Trump's bad behavior one time,
you get to co-host a podcast

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:38.537
with Obama
and Springsteen.

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:41.140
[As Graham]
"Fellas, I'm looking at my
Spotify, and I cannot believe

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:45.311
I am finding out like this.
Well, count me out."

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:48.781
[As Obama] "You can't be out
when you were never in."

00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:53.352
[As Springsteen]
"Yeah, Linds..."

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:57.889
Ooh.

00:05:57.889 --> 00:06:00.726
[Normal voice] I tried to get
two rock 'n' rollers.

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:04.630
And I nailed the Ringo.
That's it.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.767
You always said, "Only one
rock 'n' roller a show."

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:08.968
[As Springsteen]
"Yeah, Linds."

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.736
[Normal voice]
That was a little better.

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:11.770
[As Springsteen]
"You're out, Linds" --

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.739
[ Laughs ]

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:15.207
[Normal voice] Graham's been
all over cable news,

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:17.242
proclaiming Trump the face
of the Republican party

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:20.078
even after the insurrection
and the mass death

00:06:20.078 --> 00:06:21.647
and misery
his presidency produced.

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:24.183
Over the weekend, Graham flew to
Trump's Mar-a-Lago resort

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.252
to spend time golfing
and dining with Trump.

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:27.886
He has spoken to
the former president

00:06:27.886 --> 00:06:31.424
nearly daily since January 6th,
more frequently than

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:33.526
any of his Republican colleagues
in the Senate.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.328
They talk almost daily?

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:37.630
I don't even speak to my own
family on a daily basis.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.331
I tried to Zoom
with my dad last week,

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:40.800
but he wouldn't stop
complaining about

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.668
how much he hates
the Sea Captain.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.303
Still.
Let it go, Dad.

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:45.972
He hasn't been on the show
for months.

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:49.241
Last I heard, his crew threw him
overboard for hoarding limes.

00:06:49.241 --> 00:06:51.710
-It was Margarita Monday.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.145
-Anything else, Dad.

00:06:53.145 --> 00:06:55.581
-Samberg texted,
and wanted me to tell you

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:57.516
that Frisbee sucks.

00:06:57.516 --> 00:06:59.919
-Dude, she's here today.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.220
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.456
My bad.

00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:05.792
-I told you to leave after the
"Streetcar Named De-Liar" jokes.

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:08.160
If you're still here,
that's on you.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.328
Quiet, Frisbee.

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:11.597
Don't worry. She's not here.
we pre-tape that.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:14.032
Anyway, the point is, even after
a violent insurrection

00:07:14.032 --> 00:07:16.135
to overthrow the government,
the GOP has essentially

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:18.704
pledged its unwavering loyalty
to Trump.

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:20.906
And now, he's set to make
his first political speech

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:23.275
since leaving office
this week at CPAC --

00:07:23.275 --> 00:07:25.111
not to be confused
with CPAP,

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.645
which is what Melania
wears at night

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:27.913
so Trump won't try
to kiss her.

00:07:27.913 --> 00:07:29.415
[As Trump]
"Yeah, it's really sad.

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.183
It has something to do
with her airways.

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:33.385
It's a medical condition.

00:07:33.385 --> 00:07:34.486
Melania,
what's it called?

00:07:34.486 --> 00:07:36.455
Mel?

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:37.923
Mel?

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:40.059
What's your sleep
thing called?

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:43.996
I want to say Sleep Applejack,
but that's definitely wrong.

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:45.564
Mel?

00:07:45.564 --> 00:07:48.133
Is it Sleep Applebee's?

00:07:48.133 --> 00:07:51.070
She's sleeping bad
in the neighborhood.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.939
Did you hear that, Mel?

00:07:53.939 --> 00:07:56.342
I did a spin
on the Applebee's --

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:58.243
she probably can't hear me
over the machine."

00:07:58.243 --> 00:07:59.678
[Normal voice]
And in advance of the speech,

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:01.681
Graham has been all over
cable news,

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:04.883
talking up Trump as the leader
and the future of the party.

00:08:04.883 --> 00:08:07.719 line:0%
-Trump's gonna give a speech
Sunday that's gonna be

00:08:07.719 --> 00:08:09.355 line:0%
very policy-centric.

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:11.490 line:0%
Every Republican
should rally around it.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.625 line:0%
I think it will help us
with Independents.

00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:16.829 line:0%
And I've never felt better
about President Trump's

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:18.998 line:0%
leading the party
than I do right now.

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:21.867
-First of all, you really expect
us to believe his speech

00:08:21.867 --> 00:08:23.335
is gonna be policy-centric?

00:08:23.335 --> 00:08:25.070
His speeches
weren't even policy-centric

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.104
when he was president.

00:08:26.104 --> 00:08:27.540
I bet I can predict
what it'll be.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.109
He'll spend a half an hour
whining about getting canceled,

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:31.243
zing Cheney a few times.

00:08:31.243 --> 00:08:32.644
At some point,
he'll say a curse word,

00:08:32.644 --> 00:08:35.314
and the crowd will go nuts
like a bunch of fifth graders

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:37.717
when the music teacher says
the word "pianist" too fast.

00:08:37.717 --> 00:08:38.817
And then,
he'll mention The Squad,

00:08:38.817 --> 00:08:40.219
and everybody'll boo.

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:42.654
The whole thing is basically
"Rocky Horror Picture Show"

00:08:42.654 --> 00:08:44.090
for wingnuts.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:46.258
By the way, at the same time
that he's openly cheerleading

00:08:46.258 --> 00:08:48.594
a former president who tried
to overturn an election,

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:50.095
incited a violent
insurrection,

00:08:50.095 --> 00:08:53.232
and routinely called for his
political enemies to be jailed,

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:55.000
Graham is also calling
President Biden's

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.169
COVID relief package
"divisive,"

00:08:57.169 --> 00:09:00.372
despite the fact that it is
overwhelmingly popular in polls.

00:09:00.372 --> 00:09:03.709
Just yesterday, a poll found
that 76% of voters,

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:06.445
including 60% of Republicans,
support the bill.

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:09.048
Do you know how rare
that kind of consensus is?

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:12.284
You can't even get 76% of voters
to agree to vote.

00:09:12.284 --> 00:09:14.553
And yet, Graham had this
to say about it.

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:18.457
-All I can say is that
this $1.9 trillion

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:20.626
being jammed
in a partisan fashion,

00:09:20.626 --> 00:09:23.528
doubling the minimum wage,
and a bunch of other stuff,

00:09:23.528 --> 00:09:26.865
is the furthest thing
from unity I have seen.

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:28.234
-Really?

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:30.102
It's the furthest thing
from unity you've seen?

00:09:30.102 --> 00:09:33.071
Was your vision obstructed
from the Trump flag

00:09:33.071 --> 00:09:35.374
rioters hung
at the Capitol?

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:36.909
So, Republicans have,
for the most part,

00:09:36.909 --> 00:09:38.977
pledged complete and total
loyalty to Trump

00:09:38.977 --> 00:09:40.646
as he prepares to reemerge
for his first

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:42.080
post-presidency speech.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.982
Not only that,
Trump's lies about the election

00:09:43.982 --> 00:09:45.885
have essentially become canon
on the right.

00:09:45.885 --> 00:09:48.587
Over the weekend,
House GOP whip Steve Scalise

00:09:48.587 --> 00:09:50.756
refused to say that the election
wasn't stolen.

00:09:50.756 --> 00:09:53.959
And earlier this week, the
chairman of CPAC, Matt Schlapp,

00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:57.196
of the law firm Schlemiel
Schlimazel and Schlapp,

00:09:57.196 --> 00:09:58.931
essentially doubled down
on the lie.

00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:01.233 line:0%
-It's still very important
that we go back

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:03.034 line:0%
to the idea
of legal voting,

00:10:03.034 --> 00:10:06.138 line:0%
and people should be
legally registered to vote
in order to vote.

00:10:06.138 --> 00:10:08.173 line:0%
When voter fraud occurs,
no matter who...

00:10:08.173 --> 00:10:09.241 line:0%
-No, but you need
to have proof.

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:11.043 line:0%
-...it should be
fully prosecuted.

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:13.979 line:0%
-You have to have proof that it
would have changed the outcome.

00:10:13.979 --> 00:10:15.180 line:0%
-We have it.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:16.448 line:0%
-You don't have it.

00:10:16.448 --> 00:10:18.917 line:0%
Matt, why do you ignore
that dozens of lawsuits

00:10:18.917 --> 00:10:20.552 line:0%
failed on this?

00:10:20.552 --> 00:10:22.354 line:0%
-Why ignore it?
-You're right.

00:10:22.354 --> 00:10:24.289 line:0%
They did --
They did fail.

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:26.959 line:0%
But guess what -- you know this,
you're a good lawyer --

00:10:26.959 --> 00:10:28.627 line:0%
just because
you fail in court

00:10:28.627 --> 00:10:30.162 line:0%
doesn't mean you don't have
a good case.

00:10:30.162 --> 00:10:31.731 line:0%
It means you lost
in court.

00:10:31.731 --> 00:10:33.632
-Believe it or not,
it can be both.

00:10:33.632 --> 00:10:36.168
You can lose in court
and have a bad case --

00:10:36.168 --> 00:10:38.403
especially if you lose 60 times,
and your lawyer

00:10:38.403 --> 00:10:39.638
starts leaking
from the head

00:10:39.638 --> 00:10:41.940
like he mixed up the shampoo
and the motor oil.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.043
[As Giuliani] "Crap! No wonder
my car wouldn't start!

00:10:44.043 --> 00:10:46.779 line:0%
Oh, Rudy, this is
while your cousin left you."

00:10:46.779 --> 00:10:49.615 line:0%
[Normal voice]
And yet, as crazy as these
people are, there's no doubt

00:10:49.615 --> 00:10:51.583 line:0%
that they are
the core constituency

00:10:51.583 --> 00:10:52.952 line:0%
in the modern
Republican party --

00:10:52.952 --> 00:10:55.087 line:0%
a party that has become
totally unmoored from reality,

00:10:55.087 --> 00:10:58.757
that relishes performative
cruelty, and traffics in racism,

00:10:58.757 --> 00:11:00.726
cultural grievances,
and paranoia.

00:11:00.726 --> 00:11:02.728
Even the few
non-psychotic Republicans left

00:11:02.728 --> 00:11:03.862
are willing
to admit this.

00:11:03.862 --> 00:11:05.897
Utah Senator Mitt Romney
said this week that,

00:11:05.897 --> 00:11:08.033
if Trump runs
in 2024,

00:11:08.033 --> 00:11:09.769
he'll probably win
the nomination.

00:11:09.769 --> 00:11:12.671
-Will President Trump continue
to play a role in my party?

00:11:12.671 --> 00:11:13.705
I'm sure he will.

00:11:13.705 --> 00:11:15.340
He has, by far,
the largest voice,

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:16.875
and a big impact
in my party.

00:11:16.875 --> 00:11:18.777
I don't know if he'll run
in 2024 or not,

00:11:18.777 --> 00:11:23.915
but if he does, I'm pretty sure
he will win the nomination.

00:11:23.915 --> 00:11:25.684
-You think he would
win the nomination?

00:11:25.684 --> 00:11:27.819
-Oh, I think he'd win
the nomination if he runs.

00:11:27.819 --> 00:11:30.422
The polls show that, among
the names being floated

00:11:30.422 --> 00:11:32.825
as potential contenders
in 2024,

00:11:32.825 --> 00:11:35.794
if you put President Trump
in there, among Republicans,

00:11:35.794 --> 00:11:37.062
he wins in a landslide.

00:11:37.062 --> 00:11:39.064
And I would probably be
getting behind somebody

00:11:39.064 --> 00:11:42.201
who I thought more represented
the tiny wing

00:11:42.201 --> 00:11:44.303
of the Republican party
that I represent.

00:11:44.303 --> 00:11:45.437
-So leave the party.

00:11:45.437 --> 00:11:47.339
The distance between you
and Joe Biden is nothing

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:49.241
compared to the gulf
between you and Donald Trump.

00:11:49.241 --> 00:11:51.944
You don't have to go down with
the ship like that old couple

00:11:51.944 --> 00:11:53.278
that stayed in bed
in "Titanic."

00:11:53.278 --> 00:11:54.679
But he's right
on both counts.

00:11:54.679 --> 00:11:56.749
Trump would probably
win the nomination,

00:11:56.749 --> 00:11:59.685
and the wing of the party
that Romney represents is tiny.

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:02.488
There aren't many Romney stans
left in the GOP.

00:12:02.488 --> 00:12:05.690
Even when he was the nominee
in 2012, Republican voters

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:08.293
backed him with all
the enthusiasm of a teen

00:12:08.293 --> 00:12:11.630
who asked their parents for BTS
tickets and got Kenny G instead.

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:13.399
"Oh, I'm sorry.
I thought you love it, since,

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:15.934
you know, you play the saxophone
in marching band.

00:12:15.934 --> 00:12:18.203
I mean, look how close
you are to the stage.

00:12:18.203 --> 00:12:19.738
No good deed, I guess."

00:12:19.738 --> 00:12:21.173
This is the modern GOP --

00:12:21.173 --> 00:12:22.841
a party fully detached
from reality,

00:12:22.841 --> 00:12:24.710
and from the mainstream
of American politics.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:27.012
They're in lockstep
behind an ex-president

00:12:27.012 --> 00:12:28.880
who fomented
a violent insurrection,

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:31.316
and who oversaw a reign
of misery and mass death.

00:12:31.316 --> 00:12:33.185
But they're calling
a COVID relief bill

00:12:33.185 --> 00:12:36.321
that has 76% support from voters
"divisive."

00:12:36.321 --> 00:12:38.323
If you think that's divisive,
can you imagine

00:12:38.323 --> 00:12:40.893
what he thinks about the return
of the Sea Captain?

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:42.261 line:0%
-Oh, my God, I hate it.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:47.333
-Okay.

00:12:47.333 --> 00:12:51.203
I know we're hard on you,
Lindsey, but Jesus.

00:12:51.203 --> 00:12:52.905
This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:12:56.475 --> 00:12:58.009
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:12:58.009 --> 00:13:00.279
